{"code":"25-4031.00","title":"Library Technicians","description":"Assist librarians by helping readers in the use of library catalogs, databases, and indexes to locate books and other materials; and by answering questions that require only brief consultation of standard reference. Compile records; sort and shelve books or other media; remove or repair damaged books or other media; register patrons; and check materials in and out of the circulation process. Replace materials in shelving area (stacks) or files. Includes bookmobile drivers who assist with providing services in mobile libraries.","jobZone":3,"kinds":{"R":{"score":3.08,"share":0.1503},"I":{"score":2.7,"share":0.1228},"A":{"score":1.59,"share":0.0426},"S":{"score":4.07,"share":0.2218},"E":{"score":1.88,"share":0.0636},"C":{"score":6.52,"share":0.3988}},"highPoints":["C","S"],"tasks":[{"id":1688,"text":"Reserve, circulate, renew, and discharge books and other materials.","core":true,"importance":4.32,"relevance":90.15,"frequency":5.82},{"id":18511,"text":"Answer routine telephone or in-person reference inquiries, referring patrons to librarians for further assistance, when necessary.","core":true,"importance":4.27,"relevance":79.38,"frequency":5.39},{"id":18510,"text":"Help patrons find and use library resources, such as reference materials, audio-visual equipment, computers, and other electronic resources and provide technical assistance when needed.","core":true,"importance":4.18,"relevance":96.99,"frequency":5.08},{"id":1696,"text":"Deliver and retrieve items throughout the library by hand or using pushcart.","core":true,"importance":4.16,"relevance":92.14,"frequency":5.21},{"id":1699,"text":"Process print and non-print library materials to prepare them for inclusion in library collections.","core":true,"importance":4.12,"relevance":74.97,"frequency":3.98},{"id":18512,"text":"Catalogue and sort books and other print and non-print materials according to procedure and return them to shelves, files, or oth